  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "The budget (200/200 evals) and round cap (4/4) are exhausted, so this is the final round. The `pipelined` family successfully mapped a feasible Pareto front (18 designs) that satisfies both constraints: throughput >= 250 MSPS (best 273, front range 257-264) and max_abs_err <= 2^-13 (front range 13.4-16.2 bits). The front spans a useful trade-off space from 1002 LUTs/13.4 bits to 1373 LUTs/16.2 bits, providing a clear selection path for the 'min luts' objective. Other families (`unrolled_k`, `pipelined_m`) failed to meet the throughput constraint, confirming `pipelined` is the only viable architecture for this spec. No further exploration is possible or needed."
